  "title": "Party/PC inherited visibility transition verification",
  "baselineCommit": "3de7619f4f8385ccad0682e3543539aff908d4d3",
  "method": [
    "Real Quetzal and Emerald saves loaded through the browser file input, with genuine cached fonts, sprites and Pokemon API responses.",
    "Real tab clicks; requestAnimationFrame reads computed visibility of every descendant inside the inactive storage panel and hidden editor, plus live CSS visibility transitions. No reduced-motion setting or animation disabling.",
    "Geometry tracks main, tablist and editor x/y/width/height, scroll position, document height and width. Tests include both directions, rapid eight-switch sequences, and populated/empty desktop editor states.",
    "The matrix covers both games at 1440x1080 and 393x852 before a final Nature transition-property precedence cleanup. The focused final run repeats desktop Quetzal switches, empty editor, and checks all six Nature pills on the exact committed source.",
    "Full reconstructed save bytes and input-file SHA256 values are compared before and after navigation; no save edits are made.",
    "Images are unmodified Chromium DevTools screencast frames from the before and matrix runs. They are examples during switching, not captures synchronized to identical elapsed timestamps."
  ],
